# Unix line endings in the working tree on every OS: the scripts run on the head unit
* text=auto eol=lf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.png binary
*.gif binary
*.mgu binary
*.tgz binary
kit/renderd/prebuilt/mgu-renderd binary
*.pack binary
*.json.gz binary

# export-ignore: left out of `git archive` and of the tarball GitHub serves for a
# branch/tag, which is what a repo-tree source (mgu-repo.json) downloads and the
# head unit builds from. The store treats a tool (component.json, no build step)
# as "the repository": a tool update re-downloads that tarball, so what is in it
# is the price of every component update, not the component's own size.
#
# 20 MB of README screenshots and animations (docs/media, docs/screens) are read
# by nothing but the markdown on github.com, which shows them from the tree, not
# from an archive. Keep them out of the tarball: the CarLife tool is 0.5 MB and
# its update was 64 MB because of files like these.
/docs export-ignore
/docs/** export-ignore
